The structure of lavaan objects is never guaranteed (it's written down somewhere, I forget where, but Yves also says this quite often) so you should never rely on it staying the same (and if you do rely on it, you shouldn't be surprised if your code breaks; and you shouldn't be surprised if your code doesn't break but silently gives you the wrong result*). If you use the functions provided with lavaan, you'll always be OK.

Good luck!

Jeremy

