> It appears that during the most recent changes to lavaan, the list containing the summary statistics from summary(model_out, fit.measures = T) is now referenced with $fit instead of $FIT. Was this intended?

Unlike other (simpler) model objects in R, the summary() method for a lavaan-class object was never intended to produce a result beyond printing something readable to the Console.  Its internal structure has changed numerous times, and it originally did not even return anything at all.  summary() simply calls other lavaan functions, which you can call explicitly, most notably parameterEstimates(..., output = "pretty") and fitMeasures(..., output = "pretty")

