On 8/10/22 13:58, Shu Fai Cheung wrote:
> sem() calls lavaan(), and lavaan() will call lavaanify() if necessary.

That is correct.

> So, strictly speaking, sem() set some arguments (e.g., int.ov.free =
> FREE) and the call lavaan(), and then these argument values will be
> passed to lavaanify() if it is called. sem() itself does not call
> lavaanify() directly.

Indeed!

If you wish to call lavaanify() directly, using the same 'default'
settings as you would get from sem() or cfa(), you can use
lavaanify(model, auto = TRUE)

Yves.

